{"id":44,"date":"2011-09-13T14:26:29","date_gmt":"2011-09-13T14:26:29","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.wordpress.com\/?p=44"},"modified":"2021-01-06T12:21:57","modified_gmt":"2021-01-06T12:21:57","slug":"controllers-arduino","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/controllers-arduino\/","title":{"rendered":"Controllers (Arduino)"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><a href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/8.jpg\"><img data-attachment-id=\"45\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/8\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/8.jpg?fit=600%2C600&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"600,600\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"8\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/8.jpg?fit=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/8.jpg?fit=600%2C600&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-45\" title=\"8\" alt=\"arduino\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/8.jpg?w=300&#038;resize=300%2C300\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/8.jpg?w=600&amp;ssl=1 600w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/8.jpg?resize=150%2C150&amp;ssl=1 150w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/8.jpg?resize=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1 300w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/8.jpg?resize=100%2C100&amp;ssl=1 100w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><a href=\"http:\/\/www.arduino.cc\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arduino<\/a> is an i\/o-board, where you can connect a wide variety of sensors, motors, speakers etc. and make them talk with a computer. There are other similar concepts around, such as <a href=\"http:\/\/www.phidgets.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Phidgets<\/a>, <a href=\"http:\/\/www.eowave.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Eobody<\/a> and <a href=\"http:\/\/shop.electrotap.com\/products\/teabox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Teabox<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>What is great with this concept is that you\u2019re not limited to a products intended usage, you can buy or find and kind of sensors and attach them, so the possibilities are quite extensive.<\/p>\n<p>I have experimented with a force sensor attached to the leg of my drum chair, so, when I lean slightly backwards, I could trigger for example a looper to start recording. This has the advantage of not having to stop playing to start the looper, but it would be hard to do it in time, unless I quantize it to a transport control and play on a click.<\/p>\n<p>I have also tried to attach sliders and knobs to my snare for quick access, but then again, I would have to use my hand. It\u2019s more practical than the launchpad and I could implement visual feedback using LED\u2019s.<\/p>\n<p>I will continue working with this concept.<\/p>\n<p>More info on sensors and i\/o-boards at <a href=\"http:\/\/www.sensorwiki.org\/doku.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">sensorwiki<\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendere